<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Central and Southern Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Kasanje</h1><p class="st-meta">1620 CE – 1912 CE (approx.) · capital Kasanje</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">An Imbangala kingdom on the Kwango whose fair channelled captives from the Lunda interior to Portuguese Luanda for two centuries.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Kasanje was founded around 1620 by an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imbangala">Imbangala</a> warband, formerly allied with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/portuguese-angola">Portuguese Angola</a>, which settled in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baixa-de-kasanje">Baixa de Kasanje</a>, the fertile <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kwango-river">Kwango</a> valley. Its leader, Kasanje, and his successors combined Imbangala military traditions with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mbundu">Mbundu</a> lineage institutions to build a stable kingdom.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The king, titled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jaga">Jaga</a> Kasanje, ruled through officials drawn from different lineages, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imbangala">Imbangala</a> rituals shaped kingship. The kingdom's wealth came from its position as middleman: captives and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-trade">ivory</a> from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/lunda-empire">Lunda Empire</a> passed through the Kasanje market to Portuguese traders, who kept a resident agent there. Kasanje jealously blocked direct contact between the coast and the interior.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-slave-trade">slave trade</a> undermined Kasanje's economy, and wars with the Portuguese in the 1850s weakened it. Portuguese forces finally occupied the region in 1912, absorbing it into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/portuguese-angola">Portuguese Angola</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1620 CE – 1912 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Central and Southern Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:91.94%;width:5.81%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1620 CE – 1912 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kasanje</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Traditional Mbundu and Imbangala religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Kimbundu</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/angola">Angola</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kasanje, Cassange, Imbangala kingdom</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1766&amp;focus=kingdom-of-kasanje" aria-label="Kingdom of Kasanje on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5180 2639 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Kasanje lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5662 2807h0M5366 2764h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5500 2895h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5500 2895h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Angola. <a href="/atlas?year=1766&amp;focus=kingdom-of-kasanje">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
